{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on this trip's own telemetry. The GPS trace measures the polyline actually driven at 54.16 km against a booked optimal of 36.0 km, an excess of 18.16 km, and 18.16 km is both greater than 0.8 km and 50.44% of the optimal, so both limbs of the establishment test pass and the excess is in addition a MATERIAL deviation. The excess is measured from gps_trace.trace_distance_km, which governs over the rounded trip_record copy under POL-RD-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00105", "EV-TRIP-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the bundle picks the deviation up as a rider-requested detour. The chat log holds two rider queries and one non-answer from the driver, no waypoint_hint is set on any message, and no place or road is named by the rider, so the corroboration test in POL-RD-04 cannot be run on the record and that clause is unavailable to the driver. No pickup or dropoff amendment is recorded either: pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 has no purchase and the 36.0 km booked optimal stands as the baseline.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00105", "EV-TRIP-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "dispute.evidence.EV-CHAT-00105.payload.messages"
    },
    {
      "text": "The burden has shifted to the driver and he has not discharged it. The three primary artifacts all carry the trip identifier TRP-00105, and the rider has shown an excess over threshold on an unimpaired trace, so under POL-RD-08 the driver must point to a specific artifact and a specific clause to invoke POL-RD-03, POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 or POL-RD-12. He has pointed to none, and a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the burden.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00105", "EV-GPS-00105", "EV-FARE-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's stated excuse - 'Traffic was heavy on the PIE so I used another way' - cannot be tested against anything, because no traffic advisory covers this trip. The sole advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00105-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and no payload: its own admissibility detail records that no LTA advisory covers the PIE eastbound in the 14:26-15:44 window on 15 July 2026, and the driver's assertion names no artifact. Under POL-RD-13 the assertion is tested against the advisory for this trip and nothing else; with no such advisory the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because the driver cites no advisory evidence ID, the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle and not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so it does not trigger escalation; the deviation simply stands at the measured figure and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00105-01", "EV-CHAT-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "dispute.counterparty_statement.text",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is not impaired, so nothing stands between the rider and the measured figure. It carries 427 fixes at a 10 second sampling interval, coverage_pct of 100.0, zero gaps and a max_gap_sec of 0.0, so none of POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is met and no corroboration requirement arises. The fare_breakdown's billed 54.2 km is not needed as an independent source, and the trace's 54.16 km independently corroborates it in any event.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00105", "EV-FARE-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "payload.gaps",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The money follows arithmetically. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs: recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 36.0 + 0.28 x 42.0) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee = (3.80 + 27.00 + 11.76) + 0.80 = 43.36, with no ERP, toll or airport surcharge line to add because the optimal route carries zero ERP and this trip terminates at Changi rather than originating there. Charged_total is 65.13, so the refund is 65.13 - 43.36 = 21.77, which is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and rounds up to SGD 21.80. No exculpatory clause reduces the excess, so the computation runs against the booked 36.0 km optimal.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00105", "EV-TRIP-00105", "EV-GPS-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The engine agrees with that arithmetic to the cent and the rider does not contest it: the fare_breakdown's own derived block returns a recomputed_fare of 43.3600 and a refund_before_rounding of 21.7700, payable 21.80, which is 33.43% of the 65.13 charged. I therefore do not put the rider to proof on the quantum of the partial refund, and I record that the figure is traceable line by line and re-checkable by hand rather than a round-number goodwill payment.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.quantum",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The quantum the rider asked for is a full refund of the whole 65.13, and POL-RD-06 is what makes that more than a wish: the driver's profile records deviation_flags_90d of 4, which is 3 or more, so a pattern is ESTABLISHED on the clause's own primary test. The profile artifact is IMPAIRED - issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT, snapshot taken 2026-07-11T08:00:00+08:00, 108 hours before filing against a 72 hour threshold, weight_multiplier 0.75 - and I disclose that, but the finding survives the discount because the count is 4 against a threshold of 3. Only deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d are relied on for this test; prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter and I do not use it. Because this trip's deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on the trip's own evidence, POL-RD-06(b) licenses FULL_REFUND of charged_total of 65.13 rather than the POL-RD-02 partial, and the ruling should state the POL-RD-02 figure of 21.80 and the uplifted figure of 65.13 side by side so the size of the uplift is visible. POL-RD-06(c) additionally requires the case to be referred to driver-conduct review.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00105", "EV-GPS-00105", "EV-TRIP-00105", "EV-FARE-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-DPROF-00105.payload.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "No pass-through or billing-integrity line needs to be unpicked here, and I say so because it would be easy to invent one. erp_gantries is empty and the derived ERP block reports zero on-route and zero off-route, so POL-RD-09(1) has nothing to double-count and POL-RD-09(2) has nothing to cap; and the airport_surcharge line is 0.0, which is correct rather than defective, because the Changi surcharge applies to trips originating at the airport and this trip ends there. The refund is therefore not entangled with any third-party line.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00105", "EV-GPS-00105"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 65.13,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct review: refer DRV-00932 to driver-conduct review on the established repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d = 4 over completed_trips_90d = 344, against a threshold of 3 flags), on a trip found to be a MATERIAL deviation of 18.16 km on its own telemetry."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your route-deviation claim is upheld, and you receive the whole contested fare back.\n\nLiability. The 10-second GPS trace for TRP-00105 (EV-GPS-00105, unbroken, 427 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 sec) measures the driven polyline at 54.16 km against the 36.0 km booked optimal route on EV-TRIP-00105 — an excess of 18.16 km, which is over 20% of optimal and over 0.8 km, and is also over both 50% and 8.0 km, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL under POL-RD-01. The trace figure governs over the rounded 54.2 km copy, as POL-RD-01 requires. Nothing excuses it: there is no rider-requested detour and no rider place or road in the chat log (EV-CHAT-00105 holds two rider queries and one non-answer, with waypoint_hint null on every message), so POL-RD-04 cannot be run and is unavailable; and no pickup or dropoff was amended (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null, amended_optimal_distance_km is null), so POL-RD-05 has no purchase and the 36.0 km baseline stands. The trip is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply, and the fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not apply.\n\nThe arithmetic. Under POL-RD-02 read on the METERED fare_breakdown (EV-FARE-00105), recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 36.0 km + 0.28 x 42.0 min) x the 1.0 surge_multiplier recorded on the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee = 43.36, with no ERP, toll, surcharge or waiting line to add. Charged_total is 65.13, so the POL-RD-02 refund is 65.13 - 43.36 = 21.77, rounded up to SGD 21.80 payable — above the 0.50 de minimis and 33.4% of the charge, so POL-RD-02 alone would not reach the 90% that FULL_REFUND needs. I state that figure so the uplift below is auditable.\n\nWhy the whole fare. You asked for the full 65.13, and POL-RD-06 is what carries it. Your driver's profile records deviation_flags_90d of 4 against a threshold of 3, so a repeat-deviation pattern is ESTABLISHED on the clause's own primary test, and because this trip's deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on the trip's own telemetry, POL-RD-06(b) uplifts the remedy from the 21.80 partial to a FULL_REFUND of the 65.13 charged (no government-set or third-party pass-through lines are present to be held back). The two figures side by side: POL-RD-02 figure 21.80; POL-RD-06(b) uplifted figure 65.13.\n\nTo the driver: your explanation that traffic was heavy on the PIE is not supported by anything in the bundle. No traffic advisory covers this trip — EV-ADVIS-00105-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 — and you named no evidence ID for one. Under POL-RD-13 the assertion is tested against the flight's advisory and nothing else, so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and a general assertion of bad traffic unsupported by an advisory ID carries no weight under POL-RD-08. It neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal. Because you cited no advisory, the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so the case is decided on the money rather than escalated with the amount held. The GPS trace is not impaired for policy purposes (no gap over 90 sec, no jump over 500 m, no sampling interval over 30 sec), so POL-RD-07 imposes no corroboration requirement and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. The remaining POL-RD-10 triggers do not fire: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, the timestamps are consistent and run forward, and no charge line lacks a counterpart (the nil airport surcharge is correct, because the Changi surcharge attaches to trips ORIGINATING at the airport and this one terminates there, and erp_gantries is empty).\n\nOn the profile evidence. The pattern finding rests on EV-DPROF-00105, which the pre-pass marked IMPAIRED at weight_multiplier 0.75 with issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT (snapshot 108 hours before filing against a 72-hour threshold). The finding survives the discount, because 4 flags clear the threshold of 3, but under POL-GEN-02 the impairment caps confidence in this pattern-dependent remedy at 0.75. Only deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d were used for the test; prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter and is context only, not a ground.\n\nNo billing-integrity referral arises under POL-RD-09(4): there is no phantom gantry line and no wrongly applied surcharge. The one referral is required by POL-RD-06(c).",
    "amount_sgd_notes": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver's stated excuse - 'Traffic was heavy on the PIE so I used another way' - cannot be tested against anything, because no traffic advisory covers this trip. The sole advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00105-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and no payload: its own admissibility detail records that no LTA advisory covers the PIE eastbound in the 14:26-15:44 window on 15 July 2026, and the driver's assertion names no artifact. Under POL-RD-13 the assertion is tested against the advisory for this trip and nothing else; with no such advisory the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because the driver cites no advisory evidence ID, the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle and not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so it does not trigger escalation; the deviation simply stands at the measured figure and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal route.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00105-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The driver's explanation for the detour ('traffic was heavy on the PIE') names no advisory and cites no evidence id, so it is weightless under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-03 is unavailable; but the very same fact means the absent advisory EV-ADVIS-00105-01 (status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0) is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact and does not fire the mandatory escalation in POL-RD-10(5) - a party cannot invoke an artifact it never cited. The case is therefore decided on the money at the POL-RD-02 figure rather than escalated with the disputed amount held.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00105-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
