    ],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "To both parties — the rider is refunded the whole SGD 65.13 charged.\n\nDistance. The governing measurement is the GPS trace EV-GPS-00105, which reads 54.16 km, not the rounded 54.2 km convenience copy on the trip record EV-TRIP-00105. Against the booked optimal of 36.0 km that is an excess of 18.16 km, which clears both establishment tests (more than 0.8 km and more than 20% of optimal) and is additionally MATERIAL (over 50% and over 8 km). The trace is unbroken — 427 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s — so POL-RD-07 does not impair it and nothing stands between the rider and the measured figure.\n\nExculpation. There is none. The driver's explanation that traffic was heavy on the PIE points to no artifact; the only advisory, EV-ADVIS-00105-01, is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 with no payload, so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. That absence is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so it does not by itself escalate the case under POL-RD-10(5). The chat log EV-CHAT-00105 holds two rider queries and one non-answer, no waypoint_hint is set and no place is named, so POL-RD-04 cannot be run; pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 has no purchase. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not apply.\n\nMoney on the POL-RD-02 arithmetic. Charged_total is SGD 65.13. The recomputed fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 36.0 + 0.28 x 42.0) x the 1.0 surge multiplier read from the fare_breakdown EV-FARE-00105) + 0.80 platform fee = (3.80 + 27.00 + 11.76) + 0.80 = SGD 43.36. The refund is 65.13 - 43.36 = SGD 21.77, rounded up to SGD 21.80 — 33.4% of the charge, short of the 90% that would itself make FULL_REFUND available under POL-RD-02. POL-RD-09 adds nothing: ERP is nil with no gantry lines and no phantom charge, and the nil Changi surcharge is correct because that surcharge attaches to trips ORIGINATING at the airport while this trip ends there. So the POL-RD-02 figure is SGD 21.80.\n\nThe uplift, and the driver's objection to it. Because this is a MATERIAL deviation substantiated on this trip's own evidence, and the driver's profile EV-DPROF-00105 records deviation_flags_90d of 4 — established at 3 or more — POL-RD-06(b) lifts the remedy from the SGD 21.80 partial to FULL_REFUND of the SGD 65.13 charged. Side by side, as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 figure SGD 21.80; uplifted figure SGD 65.13. The driver's claim that the uplift rests entirely on an impaired artifact is correct as to the artifact and I say so openly: EV-DPROF-00105 is IMPAIRED at weight_multiplier 0.75 with issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT (snapshot taken 108 hours before filing against a 72-hour threshold). The finding survives the discount because the count is 4 against a threshold of 3, and only deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d are used for it — prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter and is context only, as the rider's own claim concedes. The impairment does, however, cap my confidence at 0.75; that is still above the platform-wide floor of 0.70, so the case is decided rather than escalated.\n\nReferral. POL-RD-06(c) additionally requires the matter to go to driver-conduct review. That referral rides with the money and does not delay or suppress it."
  },
